-- title:
--   Normality of the descended special fibre B₀/π₀B₀
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a level $M'\neq 0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)(M')$ over the residue field of $A$, an inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base-changed modular function field of level $M'$ into the $x_H$-function field of level $(q^2M',\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, a constant-reduction datum $R_0$ for $A$ between these two fields (a valuation subring with surjective residue map, a map on places and the compatibilities recorded in `ConstantReduction`), a member $s$ of $W$, and the frame data: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with elements $\pi_0$ (lying in $A$), $\zeta_0$, $\varpi_t$, $\xi$, a natural number $\ell$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by $A$ and an element $\varpi_b$, a prime $\ell'$, an intermediate field $K_{\ell}$ of $k_0\subseteq k_0((t))$ which is an algebra over $A'=A\cap k_0$ compatibly with $k_0$, a nonzero $j_\ell\in K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t'\in A'$, an ideal $y$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A'\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, a subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ over $A'$ contained in a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$, naturals $n,m$, $\gamma_0\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A'$ at its maximal ideal, the condition $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\in K_\ell$, an element $a_0\in A'$, a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$, and a term $\mathcal F$ of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.RigidDescentHyps`](def/ModularCurve_RigidDescentHyps.html#L28) for all of these. Let $G$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}(q\ell')M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$, i.e. $\tau$ transforms $q$-expansion quotients of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ as the $\gamma^{-1}$-translate does, under any embedding of $k_0$ in $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$; let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$, let $B_0$ be the $A'$-subalgebra of elements of $B_t$ fixed by $G$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ induced by $W_t$. Then the quotient of $B_0$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$ is integrally closed.
--
--   This is the normality of the special fibre of the descended supersingular chart in the stable-reduction analysis of the modular curve of level $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$: after reduction the invariant ring $B_0/\pi_0B_0$ is identified with a ring of invariants of the coordinate ring of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$ under a finite group of scalars, which is a Dedekind domain. It feeds the formal smoothness statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.formallySmooth_invariants_of_rigidChart_framed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.formallySmooth_invariants_of_rigidChart_framed) for the same frame.
